# Native Select

A styled native `select`. It opens the browser's own picker, which suits mobile screens and long option lists, and needs no JavaScript. Use `Select` when you need custom option content or search.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { NativeSelect, NativeSelectOption } from "#lib/components/ui/native-select/index.js";
</script>

<NativeSelect>
	<NativeSelectOption value="">Select status</NativeSelectOption>
	<NativeSelectOption value="todo">Todo</NativeSelectOption>
	<NativeSelectOption value="in-progress">In progress</NativeSelectOption>
	<NativeSelectOption value="done">Done</NativeSelectOption>
</NativeSelect>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/native-select.json
```

## Groups

Wrap options in `NativeSelectOptGroup` and set its `label` to group them under a heading.

<Demo section="groups" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<NativeSelect>
	<NativeSelectOptGroup label="Engineering">
		<NativeSelectOption value="frontend">Frontend</NativeSelectOption>
		<NativeSelectOption value="backend">Backend</NativeSelectOption>
	</NativeSelectOptGroup>
</NativeSelect>
```

## Binding

Use `bind:value` to read and set the selected option. Other attributes, such as `name`, `id`, `required`, and `onchange`, pass through to the `select`.

<Demo section="binding" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { NativeSelect, NativeSelectOption } from "#lib/components/ui/native-select/index.js";

	let status = $state("todo");
</script>

<NativeSelect bind:value={status}>
	<NativeSelectOption value="todo">Todo</NativeSelectOption>
	<NativeSelectOption value="done">Done</NativeSelectOption>
</NativeSelect>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, the height matches the input of the same size, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<NativeSelect size="sm">...</NativeSelect>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius that follows `size`.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<NativeSelect rounded="pill">...</NativeSelect>
```

## States

Set `disabled` to dim the select and block it. Set `aria-invalid="true"` to show the invalid ring.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<NativeSelect disabled>...</NativeSelect>
<NativeSelect aria-invalid="true">...</NativeSelect>
```

## API

`NativeSelect` extends the native `select` attributes, except the numeric `size` attribute, which is replaced by the shared size scale. The `class` goes on the wrapper that holds the select and the chevron. `NativeSelectOption` and `NativeSelectOptGroup` extend the `option` and `optgroup` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends Omit<CompPropsWithChild<"select">, "size" | "value"> {
	/** Value of the selected option; supports `bind:value` */
	value?: CompPropsWithChild<"select">["value"];
	/** Height, padding, and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
